.TH OPENOTES 1 "2026-08-31" "Openotes 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openotes \- offline-first, end-to-end-encrypted notes with WebDAV sync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openotes
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B openotes new
.BR note | notebook | reminder
.br
.B openotes open note
.B \-\-id
.I ID
.br
.B openotes open notebook
.B \-\-id
.I ID
.br
.B openotes
.I openotes://URI
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Openotes
is a desktop notes application. Notes are stored in an encrypted SQLite
database on the local machine and are never sent to a hosted service.
Synchronisation between devices is end-to-end encrypted and goes to a WebDAV
server the user supplies; backups are written locally or to that same server.
There is no account and no subscription.
.PP
Openotes is a fork of Notesnook by Streetwriters (Private) Limited, with
Notesnook Cloud replaced by WebDAV sync. It is not affiliated with, endorsed
by, or supported by Streetwriters.
.PP
Running
.B openotes
with no arguments opens the main window, or raises the window of an already
running instance. Arguments that Openotes does not recognise are ignored
rather than treated as an error, because desktop launchers and the desktop
environment add arguments of their own.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start without showing a window. The window is shown the next time
.B openotes
is run, or when an
.B openotes://
link is opened. Desktop environments use this for autostart entries, so that
the application is already running when the user first opens it.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
A command is applied when Openotes starts: the window opens directly on the
note, notebook or dialog named. If Openotes is already running, the second
launch raises the existing window and exits; only an
.B openotes://
URI is handed over to it, not a command.
.TP
.B new note
Open a new, empty note in the editor.
.TP
.B new notebook
Open the new-notebook dialog.
.TP
.B new reminder
Open the new-reminder dialog.
.TP
.BI "open note \-\-id " ID
Open the note with the given identifier. The command is ignored if
.B \-\-id
is missing.
.TP
.BI "open notebook \-\-id " ID
Open the notebook with the given identifier. The command is ignored if
.B \-\-id
is missing.
.SH URI SCHEME
Openotes registers the
.B openotes://
URI scheme with the desktop environment. A URI passed on the command line, or
opened from another application, is handed to the running instance instead of
starting a second copy.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENOTES_DATA_DIR
Absolute path to use as the application data directory, overriding the
XDG location below. Useful for keeping notes on removable media.
.TP
.B OPENOTES_PORTABLE
Set to
.B 1
to keep application data in a
.I data
directory next to the executable instead of in the user's home directory.
.B OPENOTES_DATA_DIR
takes precedence over this.
.TP
.B OPENOTES_UI_ROOT
Directory holding the built user interface. Packages set this so the
interface can live outside
.IR /usr/bin .
When unset, Openotes looks for a
.I ui
directory next to the executable.
.TP
.B OPENOTES_NATIVE_DIR
Directory holding the bundled native libraries: the encrypted SQLite build and
the two full-text-search tokenizer extensions. When unset, Openotes looks for
a
.I native
directory next to the executable.
.TP
.B OPENOTES_LOG_LEVEL
Log verbosity: one of
.BR error ", " warn ", " info ", " debug " or " trace .
The default is
.BR info .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for application data. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the cache and the log files. Defaults to
.IR ~/.cache .
.TP
.B XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR
Documents directory, used to derive the default backup location. Defaults to
.IR ~/Documents .
.PP
Openotes also reads
.BR APPIMAGE ", " FLATPAK_ID " and " SNAP ,
which the respective runtimes set, to detect how it was packaged. They are not
meant to be set by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/openotes/
Application data. Honours
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
and is overridden by
.BR OPENOTES_DATA_DIR .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/openotes/profiles/default/notesnook.db
The encrypted notes database. The file keeps its upstream name.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/openotes/attachments/
Encrypted attachment blobs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/openotes/settings.json
Application settings, including the WebDAV server configuration. Credentials
are not stored here.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/openotes/logs/app.log
The current log file. Older logs are rotated alongside it.
.TP
.I ~/Documents/Openotes/backups/
Default directory for local backups.
.PP
Under Flatpak these paths are inside
.IR ~/.var/app/org.openotes.Openotes/ ,
except backups, which stay in the real documents directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B openotes
exits
.B 0
on success, including after
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version ,
and non-zero if the application cannot start.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR xdg\-open (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
.I https://github.com/yuvalkolodkingal/notesnook
